[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From fdaba61ef8a268d4136d0a113d153f7a89eb9984 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Rik van Riel <riel@surriel.com>\nDate: Mon, 21 Jun 2021 19:43:30 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] sched/fair: Ensure that the CFS parent is added after\n unthrottling\n\nEnsure that a CFS parent will be in the list whenever one of its children is also\nin the list.\n\nA warning on rq->tmp_alone_branch != &rq->leaf_cfs_rq_list has been\nreported while running LTP test cfs_bandwidth01.\n\nOdin Ugedal found the root cause:\n\n\t$ tree /sys/fs/cgroup/ltp/ -d --charset=ascii\n\t/sys/fs/cgroup/ltp/\n\t|-- drain\n\t`-- test-6851\n\t    `-- level2\n\t\t|-- level3a\n\t\t|   |-- worker1\n\t\t|   `-- worker2\n\t\t`-- level3b\n\t\t    `-- worker3\n\nTimeline (ish):\n- worker3 gets throttled\n- level3b is decayed, since it has no more load\n- level2 get throttled\n- worker3 get unthrottled\n- level2 get unthrottled\n  - worker3 is added to list\n  - level3b is not added to list, since nr_running==0 and is decayed\n\n [ Vincent Guittot: Rebased and updated to fix for the reported warning. ]\n\nFixes: a7b359fc6a37 (\"sched/fair: Correctly insert cfs_rq's to list on unthrottle\")\nReported-by: Sachin Sant <sachinp@linux.vnet.ibm.com>\nSuggested-by: Vincent Guittot <vincent.guittot@linaro.org>\nSigned-off-by: Rik van Riel <riel@surriel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Vincent Guittot <vincent.guittot@linaro.org>\nSigned-off-by: Ingo Molnar <mingo@kernel.org>\nTested-by: Sachin Sant <sachinp@linux.vnet.ibm.com>\nAcked-by: Odin Ugedal <odin@uged.al>\nLink: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20210621174330.11258-1-vincent.guittot@linaro.org\n\ndiff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c\nindex bfaa6e1f6067..23663318fb81 100644\n--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c\n+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c\n@@ -3298,6 +3298,31 @@ static inline void cfs_rq_util_change(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq, int flags)\n \n #ifdef CONFIG_SMP\n #ifdef CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED\n+/*\n+ * Because list_add_leaf_cfs_rq always places a child cfs_rq on the list\n+ * immediately before a parent cfs_rq, and cfs_rqs are removed from the list\n+ * bottom-up, we only have to test whether the cfs_rq before us on the list\n+ * is our child.\n+ * If cfs_rq is not on the list, test whether a child needs its to be added to\n+ * connect a branch to the tree  * (see list_add_leaf_cfs_rq() for details).\n+ */\n+static inline bool child_cfs_rq_on_list(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq)\n+{\n+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;\n+\tstruct list_head *prev;\n+\n+\tif (cfs_rq->on_list) {\n+\t\tprev = cfs_rq->leaf_cfs_rq_list.prev;\n+\t} else {\n+\t\tstruct rq *rq = rq_of(cfs_rq);\n+\n+\t\tprev = rq->tmp_alone_branch;\n+\t}\n+\n+\tprev_cfs_rq = container_of(prev, struct cfs_rq, leaf_cfs_rq_list);\n+\n+\treturn (prev_cfs_rq->tg->parent == cfs_rq->tg);\n+}\n \n static inline bool cfs_rq_is_decayed(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq)\n {\n@@ -3313,6 +3338,9 @@ static inline bool cfs_rq_is_decayed(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq)\n \tif (cfs_rq->avg.runnable_sum)\n \t\treturn false;\n \n+\tif (child_cfs_rq_on_list(cfs_rq))\n+\t\treturn false;\n+\n \treturn true;\n }\n \n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n**File: `kernel/sched/fair.c`**\n1. **New Function Added**: A new inline function `child_cfs_rq_on_list` is introduced. This function checks if a child `cfs_rq` is present on the list relative to its parent `cfs_rq`.\n   - It determines if the current `cfs_rq` is on the list and retrieves the previous `cfs_rq` from the list.\n   - If the `cfs_rq` is not on the list, it checks a temporary branch to see if a child needs to be added to connect to the tree.\n   - The function returns true if the previous `cfs_rq` is a child of the current `cfs_rq`'s task group.\n\n2. **Modification in Existing Function**: The `cfs_rq_is_decayed` function is modified to include a call to `child_cfs_rq_on_list`. If a child `cfs_rq` is found on the list, the function will return false, indicating that the current `cfs_rq` is not decayed.\n\n### Relationships Between Modifications\n\nThe modifications establish a relationship between the presence of child `cfs_rq` instances on the scheduling list and the decay status of their parent `cfs_rq`. By ensuring that a parent `cfs_rq` is not considered decayed if any of its children are present on the list, the patch addresses the issue of incorrect scheduling behavior that could lead to warnings during the execution of specific tests (e.g., LTP test `cfs_bandwidth01`). This change enhances the integrity of the scheduling logic by maintaining the correct hierarchy and relationships between parent and child `cfs_rq` entities in the scheduling system."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["kernel/sched/fair.c"]}, "begin to deal with kernel/sched/fair.c in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 49}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug occurs when a `cfs_rq` (completely fair scheduler run queue) associated with a parent task group is not correctly added to the scheduling list after its child has been unthrottled, leading to an inconsistency where a child can exist on the list without its parent. This inconsistency triggers a warning related to the temporary branch of the run queue not aligning with the expected state of the leaf `cfs_rq` list.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        sched/fair: Ensure that the CFS parent is added after\n unthrottling\n\nEnsure that a CFS parent will be in the list whenever one of its children is also\nin the list.\n\nA warning on rq->tmp_alone_branch != &rq->leaf_cfs_rq_list has been\nreported while running LTP test cfs_bandwidth01.\n\nOdin Ugedal found the root cause:\n\n\t$ tree /sys/fs/cgroup/ltp/ -d --charset=ascii\n\t/sys/fs/cgroup/ltp/\n\t|-- drain\n\t`-- test-6851\n\t    `-- level2\n\t\t|-- level3a\n\t\t|   |-- worker1\n\t\t|   `-- worker2\n\t\t`-- level3b\n\t\t    `-- worker3\n\nTimeline (ish):\n- worker3 gets throttled\n- level3b is decayed, since it has no more load\n- level2 get throttled\n- worker3 get unthrottled\n- level2 get unthrottled\n  - worker3 is added to list\n  - level3b is not added to list, since nr_running==0 and is decayed\n\n [ Vincent Guittot: Rebased and updated to fix for the reported warning. ]\n\nFixes: a7b359fc6a37 (\"sched/fair: Correctly insert cfs_rq's to list on unthrottle\")\nReported-by: Sachin Sant <sachinp@linux.vnet.ibm.com>\nSuggested-by: Vincent Guittot <vincent.guittot@linaro.org>\nSigned-off-by: Rik van Riel <riel@surriel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Vincent Guittot <vincent.guittot@linaro.org>\nSigned-off-by: Ingo Molnar <mingo@kernel.org>\nTested-by: Sachin Sant <sachinp@linux.vnet.ibm.com>\nAcked-by: Odin Ugedal <odin@uged.al>\nLink: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20210621174330.11258-1-vincent.guittot@linaro.org  \n        \n        Patch:\n         #ifdef CONFIG_SMP\n #ifdef CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED\n+/*\n+ * Because list_add_leaf_cfs_rq always places a child cfs_rq on the list\n+ * immediately before a parent cfs_rq, and cfs_rqs are removed from the list\n+ * bottom-up, we only have to test whether the cfs_rq before us on the list\n+ * is our child.\n+ * If cfs_rq is not on the list, test whether a child needs its to be added to\n+ * connect a branch to the tree  * (see list_add_leaf_cfs_rq() for details).\n+ */\n+static inline bool child_cfs_rq_on_list(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq)\n+{\n+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;\n+\tstruct list_head *prev;\n+\n+\tif (cfs_rq->on_list) {\n+\t\tprev = cfs_rq->leaf_cfs_rq_list.prev;\n+\t} else {\n+\t\tstruct rq *rq = rq_of(cfs_rq);\n+\n+\t\tprev = rq->tmp_alone_branch;\n+\t}\n+\n+\tprev_cfs_rq = container_of(prev, struct cfs_rq, leaf_cfs_rq_list);\n+\n+\treturn (prev_cfs_rq->tg->parent == cfs_rq->tg);\n+}\n \n static inline bool cfs_rq_is_decayed(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq)\n {\n \tif (cfs_rq->load.weight)\n \t\treturn false;\n \n \tif (cfs_rq->avg.load_sum)\n \t\treturn false;\n \n \tif (cfs_rq->avg.util_sum)\n \t\treturn false;\n \n \tif (cfs_rq->avg.runnable_sum)\n \t\treturn false;\n \n+\tif (child_cfs_rq_on_list(cfs_rq))\n+\t\treturn false;\n+\n \treturn true;\n }\n \n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n```c\n+static inline bool child_cfs_rq_on_list(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq)\n+{\n+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;\n+\tstruct list_head *prev;\n+\n+\tif (cfs_rq->on_list) {\n+\t\tprev = cfs_rq->leaf_cfs_rq_list.prev;\n+\t} else {\n+\t\tstruct rq *rq = rq_of(cfs_rq);\n+\n+\t\tprev = rq->tmp_alone_branch;\n+\t}\n+\n+\tprev_cfs_rq = container_of(prev, struct cfs_rq, leaf_cfs_rq_list);\n+\n+\treturn (prev_cfs_rq->tg->parent == cfs_rq->tg);\n+}\n+\n+\tif (child_cfs_rq_on_list(cfs_rq))\n+\t\treturn false;\n```"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "+static inline bool child_cfs_rq_on_list(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq)", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 7626, "induce_cid": "1e3c88bdeb1260edc341e45c9fb8efd182a5c511"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 4966, "induce_cid": "671fd9dabe5239ad218c7eb48b2b9edee50250e6"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 5543, "induce_cid": "bf0f6f24a1ece8988b243aefe84ee613099a9245"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 5652, "induce_cid": "bf0f6f24a1ece8988b243aefe84ee613099a9245"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 5752, "induce_cid": "3318544b721d3072fdd1f85ee0f1f214c0b211ee"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 5775, "induce_cid": "070f5e860ee2bf588c99ef7b4c202451faa48236"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 6443, "induce_cid": "f9be3e5961c5554879a491961187472e923f5ee0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 6470, "induce_cid": "f9be3e5961c5554879a491961187472e923f5ee0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 7265, "induce_cid": "bf0f6f24a1ece8988b243aefe84ee613099a9245"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 10780, "induce_cid": "bf0f6f24a1ece8988b243aefe84ee613099a9245"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 10802, "induce_cid": "4fc420c91f53e0a9f95665c6b14a1983716081e7"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tstruct cfs_rq *prev_cfs_rq;", "file_name": "kernel/sched/fair.c", "lineno": 10891, "induce_cid": "09a43ace1f986b003c118fdf6ddf1